{
  "_comment": "Map sources the robot UI offers (vitulus_ui, served as /api/map_sources). One entry per MapProxy layer in mapproxy.yaml: layer/grid/format must match it (the tile URL is /wmts/<layer>/<grid>/{z}/{x}/{y}.<format>). kind base = one at a time under the map, overlay = independent transparent layer on top. group (bases): photo = aerial/satellite imagery, map = drawn maps; the UI lists the bases in these two groups. id is the stable key of the browser settings and of the alignment offset (offset_key: layers that share one georeference share one offset). max_zoom = finest level worth fetching (the real level of the source; the UI magnifies beyond it). native_zoom (optional, <= max_zoom) = the finest level with real detail when MapProxy serves finer levels only magnified (Google photo: z21 upscaled from z20, T17 M9-2): the UI's Auto detail stops there and magnifies itself, a phone keeps max_zoom - 1 when that is lower, min_zoom = the source draws nothing below it. attribution: a string, or {en, cs} when it has words. layer_order (overlays): under = a tone right above the background map and UNDER the robot maps (relief, slope), over = lines ON TOP of the robot maps (cadastre, contours, buildings). blend_neutral (tone overlays, 0-1 or [r,g,b]): the colour the source draws flat ground in, so flat ground leaves the picture unchanged (the UI has built-in values for hillshade and slope). Esri Wayback (esri_wb_*): earlier releases of World Imagery; the date in the name is the release, the capture date differs by place. timeline {port} (overlays): the layer has time frames on the robot's own service at that port (vitulus_precip); the UI draws past frames and nowcast from it with a slider and uses this MapProxy layer (the newest frame) only while the service does not answer. redistributable false + license_note (not used by the UI): the terms of a source allow private use only, keep it off public endpoints.",
